1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:08,427
Rolling out a SocTalk-based AI SOC: an MSSP control plane and one tenant, on your own Proxmox host.

2
00:00:08,427 --> 00:00:11,496
Start to finish, about twenty minutes.

3
00:00:12,750 --> 00:00:14,417
You need four things.

4
00:00:14,417 --> 00:00:17,296
A Proxmox host with room for the VMs.

5
00:00:17,296 --> 00:00:20,024
A Tailscale tailnet and an API key.

6
00:00:20,024 --> 00:00:22,221
An SSH key for the machines.

7
00:00:22,221 --> 00:00:24,267
And a model key for triage.

8
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:28,634
Install the launchpad binary from the GitHub releases.

9
00:00:28,634 --> 00:00:31,464
Let it verify its plugins, then start the console.

10
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:36,314
The console is a local web app.

11
00:00:36,314 --> 00:00:41,022
Point your browser at localhost, and you drive the whole rollout from three screens.

12
00:00:42,270 --> 00:00:44,947
Every machine in the run joins one tailnet.

13
00:00:44,947 --> 00:00:50,118
Add the tailnet and its key here, then test that the key works before you rely on it.

14
00:00:51,370 --> 00:00:53,330
The host is your Proxmox server.

15
00:00:53,330 --> 00:00:59,033
Choose the Proxmox platform, give it the API endpoint, and test the token before you rely on it.

16
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:05,177
The run assigns the machines to that host and takes the admin login for the control plane.

17
00:01:05,177 --> 00:01:07,060
On screen, the secrets stay masked.

18
00:01:08,310 --> 00:01:09,916
Launch starts the rollout.

19
00:01:09,916 --> 00:01:15,090
It creates the machines, joins them to the tailnet, and installs the SOC stack on each.

20
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:21,535
The install runs on its own, about fifteen minutes, mostly waiting on downloads.

21
00:01:21,535 --> 00:01:25,575
k3s and Helm, then the control plane and the tenant SOC stack.

22
00:01:25,575 --> 00:01:27,114
We fast forward past it.

23
00:01:28,360 --> 00:01:34,769
On the Proxmox host, both machines are up: the MSSP control plane and the tenant, cloned from one template.

24
00:01:36,020 --> 00:01:41,128
In the console, the tenant comes online within a minute or two, running its own SOC stack.

25
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:46,480
A built-in attack simulator runs techniques against the tenant endpoint.

26
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:49,625
Each one arrives here as an investigation, newest first.

27
00:01:50,870 --> 00:01:52,969
This is the cross-tenant fleet view.

28
00:01:52,969 --> 00:02:00,344
Every investigation gets a first pass from the model, and what it cannot close on its own becomes a pending review for an analyst.

29
00:02:01,590 --> 00:02:03,540
Start your pilot at soctalk dot A I.
